WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.579
Yep.

00:00:01.579 --> 00:00:07.560
Going to make a video about one image, in
one tweet, that simply tells us that Elden

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.929
Ring's DLC is coming.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:12.849
And it's going to be a good video too!

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:19.439
Yes, I'm going to present some truly unhinged
speculation about the contents of the DLC,

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:25.170
but more importantly, this is actually the
perfect excuse to discuss things that we haven't

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.520
dived into yet on this channel.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:37.190
Like Torrent, whose mysterious origins are
clearly being teased here..and the dark side

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:42.809
of the Erdtree, which IS absolutely a huge
part of the lore already..

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:49.120
So my goal in this video - even if my predictions
are wrong, is to at least gear you up with

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.480
some knowledge about the game's lore, that
you can take with you, no matter where the

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.410
DLC actually takes us.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.920
..and my other goal with this video is to
let you know that my art book is currently

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.280
10% off.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.309
Not gonna lie.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:08.490
But first and foremost, let's talk about who
is riding Torrent..in this image..

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:21.520
Now, at first, my mind went to it being Queen
Marika, because of that braided, golden hair.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.210
They're also riding Torrent, sitting sidesaddle,
which was historically a way for a woman to

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.860
sit on horseback with dignity, while wearing
a dress.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.340
The character is also wearing a similarly
placed upper-arm band.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:41.689
So while it's definitely possible that this
could be a young Marika, I think that's not

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:48.460
as likely as the alternative, which is that
this person is Miquella, who was one of Marika's

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.840
many demigod children.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.520
Item descriptions and dialogue all refer to
Miquella as a "he".

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:01.049
However, Miquella does have the feminine side
to match the person riding Torrent.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:06.159
Like..literally, they have a more feminine
alter-ego, called St. Trina.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:11.130
If any of this is news to you, then I recommend
you go and watch my recent 47-minute lore

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.320
video on Miquella that explains so much about
their character.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:21.700
In that video, I showed all known statues
of them, which feature them in a long garb

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.910
that cuts off at the Elbow.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.959
And looking back, this is the exact same garb
that this character is wearing.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:37.160
What's more - the hair here, while braided,
is also long and flowing..and it's identical

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.519
to Miquella's, as you can see in the opening
cinematic.

00:02:41.519 --> 00:02:47.220
Marika's, by contrast, is always symbolically
depicted as two standalone braids.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.990
Not to mention, depictions of Marika are always
of her in full womanhood, and this figure

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:55.440
is meek, and childlike by comparison.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:05.360
So 
in my eyes, this is Miquella.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.020
No question.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:15.140
If you've watched that video, you would know
that I speculate a lot about Miquella's intent

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.299
to plant a new world order..and the tweet
does say "Rise tarnished, and let us walk

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.940
a new path together".

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.879
So if we are correctly assuming that this
is Miquella, then we can also finally start

00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:30.209
to unravel the mystery surrounding Torrent,
your spectral steed.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:33.799
And that's important, because Torrent is not
just some random mount.

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:35.959
He's a full on character.

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:42.510
And for some reason, he chose you as his tarnished...down
to the very moment that he sniffs you out,

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.030
in the Stranded Graveyard.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.330
Melina is actually an unwitting part of this
plan to find, and guide you.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:54.840
She has no real memory or knowledge of whatever
plot that she's a part of, beyond following

00:03:54.840 --> 00:04:02.870
Torrent's own guidance, which she passes on
to you, with a golden ring.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:10.600
Someone who does seem to know a bit more about
Torrent is Ranni, who entrusts you with three

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:27.110
"lone wolf" spirits, and a spirit-calling
bell, which she says are "from Torrent's Former

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.110
Master".

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:34.520
Now, you could argue she's referring to Melina
as Torrent's former master..but then..that

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:41.620
doesn't really make sense, because why would
Ranni hide Melina's identity here?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.130
No.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:48.480
Torrent's former master is surely some other
third party.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.310
Someone who is clearly very in-tune with spirits,
considering Torrent is himself a spirit, and

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.990
considering the spirit-calling bell, and the
three lone wolves all stem from the same person.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:04.600
Speaking of the three-wolf spirits, there's
a relief in Farum Azula that depicts three

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.900
wolves crowded around a small, slight figure.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.720
Whoever owned torrent would have also owned
the three wolf spirits, so I always wondered

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.810
if this image was depicting Torrent's master..

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:21.650
And whoever Torrent's former master was, they
were someone that was able to compel both

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:25.590
Melina and Ranni to seek you out on their
behalf.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:30.620
My best guess, until now, was that it was
Marika doing this, as we know she goes to

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.400
great lengths to arm the Tarnished.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:39.229
Even Hewg forges weapons for you on Marika's
behalf..and he even speaks of a spirit-caller

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:44.910
he once knew..so yeah, I also thought that
this spirit-caller was Marika - until now.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:50.250
But now, considering this image, I think we
have to entertain the possibility that Torrent's

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.930
former master, could have been Miquella.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:06:00.729
Miquella had a famous ability to compel the
affection and loyalty of others..so it's also

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:07.610
very easy to think that Ranni, Melina, Torrent
and even Hewg, might have intervened to assist

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.690
you, on Miquella's behalf.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:14.320
Miquella was also a talented craftsman [Source:
Gowry Dialogue], who might have crafted the

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.550
golden spectral steed whistle ring.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:21.729
Anyway, for now, this is all just speculation..but
at the very least, we're getting closer to

00:06:21.729 --> 00:06:26.050
learning about Torrent's former master here,
for sure.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:35.720
Next, what's with the dark Erdtree in the
distance?

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:51.300
Whatever it is, it's weeping gold, and does
seem to still be a source of light, as the

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:57.840
Erdtree does in the present game, with a weak
golden light filtering from behind its branches.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:05.880
At first, I thought it might be Miquella's
Haligtree, which, as we discussed in this

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:13.460
video - IS a sort of Erdtree, though it's
an Erdtree that has already split and withered.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:16.000
So I'm not sure I buy this theory.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.110
And actualy, if you look closely, it's almost
as if there's two trees here.

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:26.560
One that is straighter, like the Erdtree,
with a streak of gold within it, and with

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:32.960
light filtering behind its branches..and another
that is twisting around it..almost as if it's

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:38.970
strangling the Erdtree, and literally sapping
the vitality from it.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:44.680
The only entity that I'd think capable of
this in the current game, would be Godwyn's

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.310
black deathroot.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:52.020
This would certainly explain the colour, the
strangling behaviour, and the sort of black

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:58.310
decay..and if Miquella is a part of this DLC,
then you'd think Godwyn would be a part of

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:04.550
things too, considering how intertwined their
histories are..but of course, this is all

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.650
just one line of speculation.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:11.849
This also raises the question of when this
event occurs.

00:08:11.849 --> 00:08:18.159
I feel like you can make valid arguments for
and against every time period.

00:08:18.159 --> 00:08:23.430
If it's in the past, that explains Miquella's
healthy state and Torrent being unsaddled

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:28.530
by you, but then it doesn't explain the state
of the Erdtree.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:32.729
If it's in the future, then it might suggest
that this takes place after you become Elden

00:08:32.729 --> 00:08:36.130
Lord, but then..what if I chose the Frenzy
ending?

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.690
How does Miquella just take Torrent from you?

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.860
Shoudn't Miquella's future be with Mohg?

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:46.920
And then there's the theory that this could
be some alternate reality altogether - past,

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.430
present, or future.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:54.810
And I quite like this idea, considering Miquella
has a whole storyline where they also exist

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:59.750
within some sort of Dreamscape, as their alias,
which is St Trina.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:04.400
Because.. the landscape here doesn't really
look like the Lands Between that we know.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:10.230
The mountains seem too low, the wheat field
seems too vast..so what if this is some sort

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.149
of spirit realm?

00:09:12.149 --> 00:09:17.760
And speaking of spirit realms, The Erdtree
being black, and the spirit graves and torrent..it

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:23.420
also reminds me of the black lampwood of the
Helphen.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:36.250
If you weren't aware, The Helphen is described
as being a sort of dark counterpart to the

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:42.680
Erdtree, in that it also offers a sort of
guidance, except its guidance is offered to

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.450
the heroic dead of the spirit world.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:54.470
We talk more about that in this video, if
you're interested in speculating down this

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.860
particular rabbit hole.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:10:04.820
But to be honest, "Shadow of the Erdtree"
is an extremely evocative title, and there

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.130
are so many things it could be referring to.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:14.779
For another example..I wonder - what if we're
supposed to reject the first impression that

00:10:14.779 --> 00:10:16.600
this image gives us?

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:21.430
Remember when Elden Ring's first cinematic
trailer dropped, and everyone thought that

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.870
Radagon was shattering the Elden Ring?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:33.410
That's what the trailer wanted you to think,
but really, he was repairing it.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:40.910
So I feel like we shouldn't rule out the possibility
that: this image might not depict the Erdtree

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.149
dying.

00:10:42.149 --> 00:10:47.310
What if this image is instead depicting a
scene from long ago, back when the Erdtree

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:50.500
was first coming into existence?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:56.870
This is an idea I put forward in my earliest
lore video for Elden Ring, and here, I stated

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:03.560
that an existing Great Tree might have been
"taken over" by the parasitic golden Erdtree.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:09.690
And while I admit that I was way too sure
of myself when presenting this theory back

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:17.380
then, I still think the theory has validity.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:23.280
We know that a crucible of chaotic life existed
within the Primordial Erdtree..and we know

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:30.010
that the crucible was related to Great Tree
ornamentation, as shown by the Crucible Knights..and

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:34.329
there are suggestions that Great Tree roots
are a distinct thing from Erdtree roots..so

00:11:34.329 --> 00:11:36.220
I'm just saying..this could be a theory to
consider.

00:11:50.839 --> 00:11:57.050
Lastly..I do also want to mention that shadow
and darkness are already kind related to the

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:12.850
Erdtree, via the Two Fingers, despite how
ironic that might sound.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:18.460
Servants of the Two Fingers were known to
cast spells such as "Darkness" and "Assassin's

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:23.160
Approach", which helped them in assassinating
the Tarnished who had strayed from the guidance

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.160
of grace.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.740
Not to mention, the Two Fingers, being these
envoys of the Greater Will, were capable of

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:34.750
bestowing beastly, living "shadows" to prominent
characters - most notably Ranni, who was given

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:41.620
Blaidd..and Marika, who was given Maliketh.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:49.649
They really could be doing anything when it
comes to the setting, and the time period

00:12:49.649 --> 00:12:52.339
of it all.

00:12:52.339 --> 00:12:57.190
But beside the Erdtree, and Torrent, and their
rider, what else do we see in this image?

00:12:57.190 --> 00:13:02.050
Well again, there are these ghostly graves
with holes in their center.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:07.399
Funnily enough, in a recent secrets video
we talked about how From Software loves reusing

00:13:07.399 --> 00:13:12.079
these cut "god's grave" assets from Dark Souls
3.

00:13:12.079 --> 00:13:18.899
And the asset actually has reappeared in Elden
Ring already - there's one at Morne Castle,

00:13:18.899 --> 00:13:20.639
where you fight the Leonine Misbegotten.

00:13:20.639 --> 00:13:21.639
They can also be found in the consecrated
snowfields.

00:13:21.639 --> 00:13:25.820
It's also not the first instance of physical
objects having a ghostly presence in the world.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.079
You can also see this in Leyndell, with the
ghostly flagpoles.

00:13:29.079 --> 00:13:32.769
And I'll be honest, I really don't know what
this means.

00:13:32.769 --> 00:13:37.329
Is it an overlap of worlds?

00:13:37.329 --> 00:13:42.740
Or are time periods persisting spiritually
somehow?

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.610
I don't know.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:48.840
And then.. you can see a couple of stone coffins
here as well.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:54.949
These appear all over the Lands Between, and
it's here that you can pick up a ton of runes,

00:13:54.949 --> 00:13:57.620
if you can get through the wolves that often
guard them.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.139
Anyway - what do you guys think?

00:14:00.139 --> 00:14:04.639
I'm getting the vibe that there's going to
be quite a long wait until Elden Ring's DLC

00:14:04.639 --> 00:14:05.639
is ready.

00:14:05.639 --> 00:14:11.589
I don't even expect a trailer any time soon.

00:14:11.589 --> 00:14:17.010
Next most likely time for a trailer might
be Summer Games Fest in early June..but then

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:22.649
they dropped this announcement on a random
tuesday, so who knows what From Software's

00:14:22.649 --> 00:14:24.250
thinking, honestly.

